.TH PDF-SMITHY 1 "2026" "PDF Smithy @PS_VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pdf-smithy \- edit PDF documents on your own machine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pdf-smithy
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ file ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B PDF Smithy
is a PDF editor for the desktop. It reorders, merges and splits pages, makes
scans searchable and straight, fills in forms, marks documents up, takes content
out for good, corrects the words on a page, converts for archiving and compares
two drafts \(em all of it locally.
.PP
The point is the last part. The usual way to do any of this is to upload the
document to a website, which for a contract, a payslip or a medical letter is
not a reasonable thing to be asked to do. Nothing here leaves the machine.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I file
Opens the given documents. Several files open as one, in the order named, which
is how merging starts.
.TP
.B --help
Shows the standard Qt and KDE options as well as these.
.SH FEATURES
.TP
.B Pages
Reorder by dragging, across several documents at once. Rotate, duplicate,
delete, extract, crop, and arrange several to a sheet. Every step is undoable.
.TP
.B Text recognition
Turns a scan into something selectable without re-rendering the page: the image
bytes that went in come back out, with the recognised words laid over them
invisibly.
.TP
.B Redaction
Content is taken out of the file rather than painted over. Text goes character by
character so the rest of the line survives; a picture that overlaps is edited
pixel by pixel.
.TP
.B Comments
Highlight, underline, strike out, boxes, ovals, lines, freehand, text boxes and
notes, each written with its own appearance so it looks the same in every
reader. They can be exported on their own as XFDF \(em sending back a marked-up
contract otherwise means sending the contract.
.TP
.B Forms
Fill in official forms and, when the answers are final, make them permanent.
.TP
.B Correcting text
Fix a typo, a date or a name in the page's own font. It says plainly what it will
not do: there is no reflow, because a PDF does not record which line follows
which.
.TP
.B Archiving and comparing
Convert to PDF/A for long-term keeping, look for what would stop a file being
archival, and see what changed between two drafts side by side.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/pdf-smithyrc
Window geometry, toolbar layout and recent files.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pdf-smithy-cli (1)
.PP
Everything the window can do to a document, the command line can do too.
.SH AUTHOR
Tom Bueng <tombueng@gmail.com>
